      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2010-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We have that \\[ \\begin{aligned}100(100 - 3) &= 100 \\cdot 97 \\\\&= 9700\\end{aligned} \\] and \\[ \\begin{aligned}100 \\cdot 100 - 3 &= 10000 - 3\\\\ &= 9997.\\end{aligned} \\]\n\nAs such, their difference is: \\[ 9700 - 9997 = - 297. \\]\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Expand both terms before subtracting",
        "Most of the \\(100\\cdot100\\) terms cancel"
      ],
